# Memory Vault — Agent Contract

> Read this file before writing anything into this vault.
> Owner: {{NAME}} · Created: {{DATE}} · Generated by agent-memory-kit

## What this is

This vault is the **single source of truth** for facts. Not a scratchpad, not a
transcript dump. If something is worth remembering, it belongs in a note here —
because this is the only place that survives a closed session.

## Structure

| Prefix | Purpose | Rule |
|---|---|---|
| `00-index.md` | The only entry point | Read this first, always |
| `01-projects` | Active work | One note per project |
| `03-preferences` | How I want things done | Only durable preferences |
| `04-decisions` | Decisions plus the reason | Append-only, never rewrite history |
| `05-reviews` | Retrospectives | One file per day/week |
| `10-archive` | Finished or dead work | Move, do not delete |
| `20-notes` | Reference material | No project home |
| `30-outputs` | Things that left the building | Link back to the source note |
| `90-templates` | Note shapes | Copy out, never edit in place |

The number is the category. Do not invent new prefixes; if a note fits nowhere,
it goes in `20-notes` and you add a line to the index.

## Non-negotiable rules

1. **One topic per note.** If a note needs two titles, it is two notes.
2. **Titles state the conclusion**, not the topic word.
   Bad: `Auth notes`. Good: `JWT refresh fails silently when clock skew exceeds 30s`.
3. **Link with `[[wikilinks]]`.** Any note that mentions another concept gets the
   link. A note with zero inbound and zero outbound links is dead weight.
4. **Update the index when you add a note.** A note not in `00-index.md` does not
   exist. Nobody browses folders.
5. **Never duplicate content across layers.** If a fact lives here, the discipline
   file gets a one-line pointer, not a copy.
6. **Search before reading.** Grep `00-index.md` first. Reading the whole vault to
   answer one question burns context for nothing.

## Writing protocol

When you learn something worth keeping:

1. Grep the index for an existing note on this topic.
2. If it exists, edit that note and add a line to its `## History` section with
   the date and what changed.
3. If not, create the note from `90-templates/note.md`, add one index line, and
   link it from at least one related note.
4. If the fact contradicts an existing note, do **not** silently overwrite. Note
   the contradiction in both places and say so in your reply.

## What must never happen

- Empty placeholder files created to "look complete"
- Notes outside the numbered structure
- Secrets, keys, or credentials written into any note
- Content copied wholesale from a conversation transcript
- An index line pointing at a file that does not exist
